@startuml 00-overview
!include ../_style/class.iuml
title Backend — the features and what links them (16.10.2026)

package "Accounts\n(01-accounts)" as Accounts {
    class loginService
    class signupService
    class accountService
}
package "Saved searches\n(02-saved-searches)" as Saved {
    class customSearchService
}
package "Search\n(03-search)" as Search {
    class newsService
}
package "Ingestion\n(04-ingestion)" as Ingestion {
    class ingestService
    class feedService
    class taggingService
    class directoryService
}
package "Sources\n(05-sources)" as Sources {
    class sourceService
    class recommendationService
}
package "Profile\n(06-profile)" as Profile {
    class profileService
}
package "Discovery\n(07-discovery)" as Discovery {
    class discoveryService
}
package "Briefing\n(08-briefing, 08b-briefing-cards)" as Briefing {
    class briefingService
    class feedbackService
}
package "E-mail\n(09-email)" as Email {
    class briefingMail
    class mailer
}
package "Following\n(10-following)" as Following {
    class entityService
}

signupService --> profileService : prepares and stores\nthe first profile
profileService --> discoveryService : looks for sources\nfor the profile
profileService --> feedbackService : sources left out
discoveryService --> sourceService
discoveryService --> ingestService : reads the\nfeeds found
discoveryService --> feedbackService
recommendationService --> feedbackService
briefingService --> discoveryService : prunes the\nsources that bring nothing
briefingService --> feedbackService : thumbs as examples
briefingService --> ingestService : searches of\nthe interests
briefingService --> entityService : news and names\nof what is followed
briefingService --> briefingMail : sends the cards
briefingMail --> mailer
newsService --> ingestService : Google News asked\nthe sentence
newsService --> feedService
ingestService --> feedService
ingestService --> directoryService : more media\nevery 20 minutes
entityService ..> taggingService : reads the names it found\nand linked to Wikidata

note as Legend
    Every request goes router → controller → service → model → Prisma (or SQL) → PostgreSQL + pgvector.
    Each package is a folder of docs/ (the number names its class diagram), with a folder per part of it.
    The shared cache (feeds, articles, stories, threads, names) is filled in background by the Ingestion,
    started with the server (server.js), and read by the Search, the Briefing and the Following.
    The AI (Ollama: gemma4:31b, deepseek-v4-pro; Gemini as fallback) is only asked on what a reader asks for:
    a profile, a search by meaning, a briefing. Database/30-database, 31-deployment and 32-a-to-z draw the rest.
end note
@enduml
